# MCP app Schemas (actions.json)

## Structure

Each action in actions.json has:
- `display_name` — Human-readable name
- `description` — What the action does
- `parameters` — JSON Schema for input (request)
- `response` — JSON Schema for output

## Parameters Schema

### Preferred: Flat Structure
- Types: `string`, `number`, `integer`, `boolean`
- All properties need `description`
- Use `required` array for mandatory fields
- Use `$schema`: "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
- Draft-07 keywords on **string** (and similar) properties are allowed where the automation UI supports them—common ones: **`enum`** (fixed allowed values), **`pattern`** (regex), **`format`** (semantic hint, e.g. `email`, `date-time`)

### String constraints (`enum`, `pattern`, `format`)
```json
{
  "parameters": {
    "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "priority": {
        "type": "string",
        "enum": ["low", "medium", "high", "urgent"],
        "description": "Ticket priority"
      },
      "order_id": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[A-Z]{2}-[0-9]{6}$",
        "description": "Vendor order id, e.g. OR-000123"
      },
      "notify_email": {
        "type": "string",
        "format": "email",
        "description": "Email to notify when the action completes"
      }
    },
    "required": ["priority", "order_id"]
  }
}
```

### Arrays of Primitives Allowed
```json
{
  "parameters": {
    "properties": {
      "ids": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": { "type": "string" },
        "description": "List of resource IDs"
      },
      "tags": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": { "type": "string" },
        "description": "Tags to apply"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Nested Objects: Flatten or Construct in server.js
If API requires nested object, accept flat params and build in server.js:
```json
{ "name": { "type": "string" }, "email": { "type": "string" } }
```
```javascript
// server.js builds: { contact: { name, email } }
```

### JSON Schema keywords: `enum`, `pattern`, `format`

`parameters` use **JSON Schema Draft 07** (see [Routing automation — custom actions / actions.json](https://developers.freshworks.com/tutorials/codelabs/routing-automation-with-custom-actions/index.html) and [`$schema` draft-07](https://json-schema.org/draft-07/json-schema-validation.html)). You may use standard validation keywords on **flat** properties:

| Keyword | Use |
|---------|-----|
| `enum` | Closed set of allowed string (or other) values |
| `pattern` | String must match a regex (JSON Schema string, not iparams) |
| `format` | Semantic formats where supported (e.g. `email`, `uri`, `date-time`) |

```json
{
  "parameters": {
    "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "priority": {
        "type": "string",
        "enum": ["low", "medium", "high"],
        "description": "Ticket priority"
      },
      "ticket_id": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[0-9]{6,12}$",
        "description": "Numeric ticket id"
      },
      "callback_url": {
        "type": "string",
        "format": "uri",
        "description": "HTTPS callback URL"
      }
    },
    "required": ["priority", "ticket_id"]
  }
}
```

Keep **MCP app constraints**: flat request parameters; **arrays of objects** in requests are not allowed — primitives and arrays of primitives only.

## Response Schema

- Nested objects allowed
- Arrays allowed
- Use `additionalProperties: true` for flexible API responses
- Include essential fields only
- Mark IDs as required; other fields optional

### Example
```json
{
  "response": {
    "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": true,
    "properties": {
      "id": { "type": "string", "description": "Resource ID" },
      "status": { "type": "string" },
      "data": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "nested_field": { "type": "string" }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Function Naming

- 2-40 characters
- Alphanumeric + underscores
- Case-sensitive — must match server.js exactly
- Cannot start with number
- No spaces, no hyphens

Valid: `createContact`, `get_ticket_status`, `fetchData123`
